# SHA-256 of every configs/claude/settings.json version tuidev has ever shipped.
# The ai-clis pack replaces ~/.claude/settings.json only when it is an
# unmodified copy of one of these (backup first); a file you edited is left
# alone. test_contract.sh fails if the current file is not listed: after
# editing it, append `settings $(shasum -a 256 settings.json | cut -d' ' -f1)`.
# settings.linux.json (what Linux installs get) is keyed `settings` too, so a
# Linux copy of any earlier release upgrades to it.
